# Fire Edition 2.1.5 seed list. Base packages remain pinned to the verified snapshot.
# Pillars
power-profiles-daemon
linux-cpupower
gamemode
# (lm-sensors, smartmontools, nvme-cli, python3-psutil/dbus/gi/apt, snapper,
#  libsnapper7t64, inotify-tools, vulkan-tools, mesa-vulkan-drivers, pciutils,
#  libnotify-bin, python3-pyqt6 already in the image)
nvtop
btop
# Grok Bot and coding agents are optional first-run installations.
# No second model runtime or model weights are carried in the ISO.
# Fireproof analysis stack
needrestart
apt-listchanges
# Privacy set moved INTO the base (Core bundle is the ISO itself)
kleopatra
tor
tor-geoipdb
torsocks
onionshare
onionshare-cli

# The Fire Edition debs themselves (built into the umbra repo by this same make run).
# Every name below is now also a Depends of shadowfetch-desktop, which is what
# shadowfetch-desktop-kde.list.chroot installs. Until 4.0.0 this list was the
# ONLY thing that put them in the image: the package graph did not describe the
# product, and `apt install shadowfetch-desktop` on any other machine got a
# Plasma desktop with no Mission Control, no Phoenix, no Fireproof and no
# Firewatch. Keeping them here is belt and braces for the chroot, not the
# declaration -- tools/ship_list_check.py fails if a package list ever again
# supplies a Shadowfetch package the graph does not reach.
shadowfetch-ember
shadowfetch-firewatchd
shadowfetch-phoenix
shadowfetch-menus
shadowfetch-control-center
shadowfetch-fireproof
shadowfetch-hwscan
